### How do you reconstruct the actual subsequence?

Start from dp[m][n] and walk backward. If the characters at positions i and j match, that character is part of the LCS; move diagonally. If they do not match, move toward the larger neighbor (up or left).

```java
package com.bank.dsa;

public class ReconstructDemo {
    public static String reconstructLCS(String a, String b) {
        int m = a.length(), n = b.length();
        int[][] dp = new int[m + 1][n + 1];
        for (int i = 1; i <= m; i++)
            for (int j = 1; j <= n; j++)
                dp[i][j] = a.charAt(i - 1) == b.charAt(j - 1)
                    ? 1 + dp[i - 1][j - 1]
                    : Math.max(dp[i - 1][j], dp[i][j - 1]);

        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();
        int i = m, j = n;
        while (i > 0 && j > 0) {
            if (a.charAt(i - 1) == b.charAt(j - 1)) {
                sb.append(a.charAt(i - 1));
                i--; j--;
            } else if (dp[i - 1][j] > dp[i][j - 1]) {
                i--;
            } else {
                j--;
            }
        }
        return sb.reverse().toString();
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println(reconstructLCS("ABCBDAB", "BDCAB")); // BCAB
    }
}
```

```text
BCAB
```

### How is this different from the Longest Common Substring?

| Aspect | Common Subsequence | Common Substring |
|---|---|---|
| Contiguity | Not required | Required |
| On mismatch | max(top, left) | Reset to 0 |
| Answer location | Corner dp[m][n] | Max anywhere |
| Gaps allowed | Yes | No |

### What are the edge cases?

If either string is empty, the LCS is 0. If both are identical, the LCS is their length. If they share no common character, the LCS is 0.

```java
package com.bank.dsa;

public class EdgeCaseDemo {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println(LongestCommonSubsequence.lcs("", "ABC"));    // 0
        System.out.println(LongestCommonSubsequence.lcs("ABC", "ABC")); // 3
        System.out.println(LongestCommonSubsequence.lcs("ABC", "XYZ")); // 0
    }
}
```

```text
0
3
0
```

### What is the time and space complexity?

Time is O(m*n). Space is O(m*n), reducible to O(min(m,n)) with rolling rows. Reconstruction requires the full table.

